{"description":"Follow-up from CTX-0292 (PR #487, issue #486). The accepted CTX-0118 decoration contract now lands as config + validation + Core px solver + runtime carry/safe-mode. Missing: live present-path painting.

Deliverable: consume Runtime::decorated_allocations() (or equivalent px frames) in the present path so gaps_out/gaps_in bands, border rings, and radius clipping are actually rendered. This requires:
1. Fractional-cell View frame composition: per-view grid/frame derivation from px frames (today the container is one global cell grid and leaves are cell rects);
2. A renderer radius primitive (FillRect has no radius/border) plus software/GPU parity and HiDPI scaling — CTX-0238g stage-2 render-owner lane owns the radius mechanism; coordinate/merge order with that task;
3. Hit-testing and input mapping updated to the decorated frames (frame for hit testing, content for painting), preserving CTX-0177 cell-gap behavior.
Acceptance: headless RGBA/frame evidence for gaps/border/radius, safe-mode 0/0/1/0 rendering, no regressions in the existing panel-gap visual tests.

